# Terminal provider strings — English (source/fallback).

terminal-display-name = terminal
terminal-description = A real shell, as a list: browse to a folder, press : for a shell there, and full-screen programs like vim open in a dashboard.
terminal-setting-shell = shell program ($SHELL is your login shell)
terminal-setting-history = shell command history
terminal-setting-scrollback = terminal emulator scrollback
terminal-setting-auto-dashboard = auto-launch dashboard for interactive programs

# Command names shown wherever the provider's commands are listed. `shell`
# swaps the folder listing for the shell, `browse` swaps back.
terminal-command-shell = shell
terminal-command-browse = folders
terminal-command-compose = write a command

# The tutorial's paragraphs about this program, under its programs section:
# <name>-tutorial, then <name>-tutorial-2 and so on, read until one is missing.
terminal-tutorial = Terminal, from the Store: press : to turn the list into a real shell running in the folder you are in, with an input line at the bottom. The header then says first command mode. Press : again to write a command in second command mode: the programs come first, then the commands you ran before. Tab completes the word you are typing, and Enter puts the command in the input line, where Enter runs it. Walk into a folder with Right first if you want the shell one level deeper. Escape returns to the folders, and full-screen programs like vim and htop get their own interactive mode.
